invariant: INV-10
file: tls_write.c
catches: tcp_blocking_key_limit
reason: ch_write never takes the step before a record, so an AES-GCM write
  key seals a data record at its last sequence number with no KeyUpdate
  first, and the next write finds the key at its ceiling. The boundary case
  counts two records where a KeyUpdate record belongs between them.

--- old
        int rc = key_update_at_ceiling(t);
        if (rc != CH_OK) {
            return rc; // it failed the session
        }
--- new
        int rc = CH_OK;
        (void)key_update_at_ceiling;
